                                    <h1>WATI vs Interakt vs Gallabox &mdash; Best WhatsApp Business Platform for D2C India 2026</h1>

                                    <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> All three are official Meta-approved WhatsApp Business Solution Providers (BSPs). <strong>Interakt wins for Shopify D2C brands</strong> (native cart abandonment + product catalogue). <strong>WATI wins for multi-channel + non-Shopify D2C</strong> (deeper automation, larger ecosystem). <strong>Gallabox wins on price</strong> (~30&ndash;40% cheaper, India-first, strong for SME D2C below &#8377;5Cr ARR). All three pass Meta&rsquo;s pricing through ('per-conversation' fee), so the platform fee is the differentiator. Below: real feature parity, pricing math, integration depth, and red flags to watch for.</p>
                                    <p>This is the honest comparison we give D2C founders evaluating WhatsApp Business platforms in 2026. We&rsquo;ve set up + run all three on client D2C accounts &mdash; with shipping volumes from 100/month to 50K+/month. Real pricing math, integration depth, automation builder UX, and the 3 cases when each absolutely wins. No vendor bias.</p>

                                    <h2>TL;DR &mdash; The Comparison at a Glance (2026)</h2>
                                    <table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Criteria</th><th>WATI</th><th>Interakt</th><th>Gallabox</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Best for</strong></td><td>Multi-channel + non-Shopify D2C</td><td>Shopify D2C</td><td>SME D2C, &lt;&#8377;5Cr ARR, India-first</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Platform fee starting</strong></td><td>&#8377;2K&ndash;&#8377;7K/mo</td><td>&#8377;2.5K&ndash;&#8377;8K/mo</td><td>&#8377;1.4K&ndash;&#8377;5K/mo</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Meta conversation fee</strong></td><td>Pass-through</td><td>Pass-through</td><td>Pass-through</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shopify integration</strong></td><td>Good</td><td><strong>Native + deep</strong></td><td>Decent</td></tr><tr><td><strong>WooCommerce</strong></td><td>Native</td><td>Native</td><td>Native</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Razorpay / Cashfree</strong></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Automation builder</strong></td><td><strong>Most powerful</strong></td><td>Strong + e-comm templates</td><td>Simpler</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Multi-agent inbox</strong></td><td>Excellent</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td><strong>API extensibility</strong></td><td><strong>Best for custom builds</strong></td><td>Strong</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td><strong>India support / GST billing</strong></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td><strong>India-native</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>

                                    <h2>Real Pricing Math (2026, Honest Breakdown)</h2>
<p>All three platforms charge: <strong>(1)</strong> a platform fee (their margin) + <strong>(2)</strong> Meta&rsquo;s per-conversation fee passed through. Meta&rsquo;s fee is the same for all platforms &mdash; <strong>~&#8377;0.30&ndash;&#8377;0.80 per user-initiated conversation, &#8377;0.65&ndash;&#8377;1.10 per business-initiated marketing</strong> conversation (rates change quarterly).</p>
<h3>Real monthly cost at typical D2C volumes</h3><table class='cmp-table'><thead><tr><th>Monthly conversations</th><th>WATI</th><th>Interakt</th><th>Gallabox</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1,000 (small D2C)</td><td>&#8377;3.5K plat + &#8377;700&ndash;1.2K Meta = ~&#8377;4.5K</td><td>&#8377;4K plat + &#8377;700&ndash;1.2K Meta = ~&#8377;5K</td><td>&#8377;2.5K plat + &#8377;700&ndash;1.2K Meta = ~&#8377;3.5K</td></tr><tr><td>5,000 (growth D2C)</td><td>&#8377;5K plat + &#8377;3.5&ndash;5.5K Meta = ~&#8377;9K</td><td>&#8377;6K plat + &#8377;3.5&ndash;5.5K Meta = ~&#8377;10K</td><td>&#8377;3.5K plat + &#8377;3.5&ndash;5.5K Meta = ~&#8377;7.5K</td></tr><tr><td>20,000 (scale D2C)</td><td>&#8377;9K plat + &#8377;14&ndash;22K Meta = ~&#8377;26K</td><td>&#8377;11K plat + &#8377;14&ndash;22K Meta = ~&#8377;28K</td><td>&#8377;7K plat + &#8377;14&ndash;22K Meta = ~&#8377;23K</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Where WATI Genuinely Wins</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Automation builder depth.</strong> Most flexible flow builder of the three. Branching, conditional logic, external API calls, JS hooks. Best for D2C brands with complex flows (multi-step quizzes, custom CRM updates, conditional offers).</li><li><strong>API + webhook extensibility.</strong> Best for technical teams building custom integrations. Webhook event coverage is broadest.</li><li><strong>Larger ecosystem of integrations.</strong> Zapier, Make (Integromat), Webhooks, native CRMs (HubSpot, Zoho, Salesforce).</li><li><strong>Multi-language broadcast tools.</strong> Important for tier-2 + regional language campaigns.</li></ul>
<h2>Where Interakt Genuinely Wins</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Shopify-native integration.</strong> Cart abandonment, product catalogue, order updates flow without setup. Built specifically for D2C ecommerce.</li><li><strong>D2C playbook templates.</strong> Pre-built abandoned cart, post-purchase, restock, win-back templates that work out-of-box for ecommerce.</li><li><strong>Native catalogue + WhatsApp Shop.</strong> WhatsApp Commerce features (catalogue browsing, product discovery, in-chat checkout) are deeper than competitors.</li><li><strong>Strong Shopify Plus support.</strong> Enterprise D2C brands on Shopify Plus get dedicated integration + support.</li></ul>
<h2>Where Gallabox Genuinely Wins</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Price.</strong> 30&ndash;40% cheaper platform fee than WATI / Interakt at similar feature parity. Wins on cost-per-conversation for SME D2C brands below &#8377;5Cr ARR.</li><li><strong>India-first build.</strong> Native GST invoicing, INR pricing, India-based support team, regional language UI.</li><li><strong>Lean automation builder.</strong> Simpler UX &mdash; easier for non-technical D2C founders to set up flows themselves.</li><li><strong>Strong with Indian CRMs.</strong> LeadSquared, Zoho CRM, Freshworks &mdash; deeper integration than competitors.</li></ul>
<h2>3 Cases Where One Absolutely Beats the Others</h2>
<h3>Interakt absolutely beats WATI + Gallabox when&hellip;</h3><p>You&rsquo;re a Shopify D2C brand running cart abandonment + post-purchase + restock flows. Interakt&rsquo;s Shopify-native integration is faster to ship + cleaner to maintain. Don&rsquo;t bother with the others.</p>
<h3>WATI absolutely beats Interakt + Gallabox when&hellip;</h3><p>You&rsquo;re running complex automation (quiz funnels, conditional offers, multi-channel coordination with email + SMS), or your stack is non-Shopify (WooCommerce + custom + headless), or you have technical team building custom integrations via webhook + API. WATI&rsquo;s automation builder is the most powerful.</p>
<h3>Gallabox absolutely beats WATI + Interakt when&hellip;</h3><p>You&rsquo;re an SME D2C brand below &#8377;5Cr ARR + cost-sensitive + want simpler UX + India-first support + GST + regional language. Save 30&ndash;40% on platform fee with minimal feature loss.</p>
<h2>4 Red Flags When Picking a WhatsApp Business Platform</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Not an official Meta-approved BSP.</strong> Use only platforms listed on Meta&rsquo;s BSP directory. Non-BSP vendors are typically reselling someone else&rsquo;s API with markup + reliability risk.</li><li><strong>Bundled Meta fee instead of pass-through.</strong> If the platform doesn&rsquo;t show you Meta&rsquo;s per-conversation fee separately, they&rsquo;re marking up Meta&rsquo;s rate. Demand pass-through pricing.</li><li><strong>No 24x7 support for outages.</strong> WhatsApp Business API breaks occasionally. Your platform&rsquo;s support response time matters when revenue depends on WhatsApp.</li><li><strong>Lock-in via custom integrations.</strong> Avoid platforms that build custom integrations into your stack that can&rsquo;t be migrated easily. Use Zapier / webhook standards.</li></ol>
