                                    <h2>FAQs</h2>
<h3>How much should I expect to spend on WhatsApp Business for D2C in 2026?</h3>
<p><strong>Platform fee: &#8377;1.5K&ndash;&#8377;11K/month</strong> depending on platform + tier. <strong>Meta conversation fee: ~&#8377;0.65&ndash;&#8377;1.10 per business-initiated marketing conversation</strong>. Total for 5K conversations/month: &#8377;7K&ndash;&#8377;10K. For 20K conversations/month: &#8377;23K&ndash;&#8377;28K.</p>
<h3>Are WATI, Interakt, and Gallabox all official BSPs?</h3>
<p><strong>Yes &mdash; all three are Meta-approved WhatsApp Business Solution Providers.</strong> Always pick from Meta&rsquo;s official BSP directory; non-BSP vendors carry reliability + compliance risk.</p>
<h3>Which integrates best with Shopify?</h3>
<p><strong>Interakt</strong> has the deepest Shopify-native integration (cart abandonment, product catalogue, order updates). WATI + Gallabox also integrate but require slightly more configuration.</p>
<h3>Which is best for WooCommerce or custom storefronts?</h3>
<p><strong>WATI</strong> has the broadest integration ecosystem + most flexible API. For non-Shopify D2C brands or custom storefronts, WATI is typically the better choice.</p>
<h3>Can I switch platforms later?</h3>
<p>Yes &mdash; WhatsApp Business numbers are portable between BSPs (with some downtime for migration). Customer chat history typically doesn&rsquo;t migrate; flows + templates need to be rebuilt. Plan migration carefully.</p>
<h3>What about Wati.io, Bird.com, Yellow.ai for D2C?</h3>
<p><strong>Wati.io</strong> is WATI (same product, different domain). <strong>Bird (formerly MessageBird)</strong> is enterprise-grade, more expensive, multi-channel. <strong>Yellow.ai</strong> is AI-conversational focused, less D2C-native. For D2C specifically, WATI / Interakt / Gallabox are the strongest fit.</p>


